Description: Constructs and analyzes networks from pairwise mutual information.
    Variables are descretized with the Freedman-Diaconis or Sturges rule,
    mutual information is estimated with a plug-in estimator and normalized by
    joing entropy, and indirect links can be pruned with the data processing
    inequality. Includes shuffled-data generation for null distributions, network
    topology and path statistics, GEXF export, and disk-backed batch and parallel
    computation for large datasets.
